README — Vivado Simulation Environment
(Directory: parser/sim/vivado/core/)

Overview
This directory contains the Vivado simulation environment for the module:

cmd_parser_slave_generic

It provides a standalone testbench for validating the parser together with the generic slave model, using XSIM (Vivado Simulator).

This README focuses only on how to run the simulation.
For architectural details, command specifications, and slave behavior, refer to the main project documentation.

Requirements
Windows 10/11

Vivado 2025.1 installed

settings64.bat available in the Vivado installation directory

MSYS2 / MINGW64 (optional, for Make)

Environment Setup
Before running any simulation, activate the Vivado environment:

Codice
vivado_env.bat
This script loads settings64.bat and prepares the Vivado toolchain.

Running the Simulation
To compile, elaborate, and run the simulation in batch mode:

Codice
make xsim
This will generate:

xsim.dir/

tb_parser_sim.wdb

log files (xsim.log, xelab.log)

Opening the GUI
To open the waveform viewer:

Codice
make xsim_gui
or:

Codice
xsim tb_parser_sim --gui
The GUI requires the previously generated xsim.dir and .wdb files.

Debug Logging
Debug messages (severity note) can be enabled through:

vhdl
constant ENABLE_DEBUG_LOG : boolean := true;
Defined in:

Codice
cmd_cfg.vhd
Warnings, errors, and fatal messages are always active.

Vivado/XSIM does not support severity filtering, so debug control is implemented directly in VHDL.

Cleaning the Directory
To remove generated files:

Codice
make clean
Additional Documentation
For complete information about:

parser architecture

command format (cmd.txt)

generic slave behavior

RAM model

byte‑enable handling

integration guidelines

please refer to the main project documentation located in the root of the repository.
